# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ardavan Mehdizadeh et al. (2025). Surface stability modeling with universal machine learning interatomic potentials: a comprehensive cleavage energy benchmarking study.
#   AI for Science. doi:10.1088/3050-287x/ae1408  arXiv:2508.21663v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2508.21663v1 (sha256 03a5364b9a7bfbd3...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 239 (Dataset/benchmark). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/mehdizadeh2025.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the 19 pretrained universal MLIPs of Table 2 and their
# cleavage-energy errors (MAE, RMSE, R2) against the DFT database of 36,718
# slabs of metallic elemental, binary and ternary compounds, with the
# single-point times per slab. Percentage errors, surface-termination
# agreement and the per-chemistry analyses are not encoded.

